ould end up outside the destination.\n    This raises :class:`~tarfile.OutsideDestinationError`."}], "claim_text": "Choosing data rejects a member whose resolved absolute path would escape the extraction destination.", "reasoning": "The data filter includes tar_filter's refusal of files whose absolute paths, after following symlinks, escape the destination.", "verdict": "SUPPORTED"}, {"citations": [{"index": 3, "quote": ".. function:: data_filter(member, path)\n\n  Implements the ``'data'`` filter."}, {"index": 3, "quote": "- For other files (directories), set ``mode`` to ``None``, so\n    that extraction methods skip applying permission bits."}], "claim_text": "For directories, data disables application of permission bits.", "reasoning": "For directories, data_filter sets mode to None so extraction skips permission bits.", "verdict": "SUPPORTED"}, {"citations": [{"index": 4, "quote": "When a filter refuses to extract a file, it will raise an appropriate exception,\na subclass of :class:`~tarfile.FilterError`.\nThis will abort the extraction if :attr:`TarFile.errorlevel` is 1 or more.\nWith ``errorlevel=0`` the error will be logged and the member will be skipped,\nbut extraction will continue."}], "claim_text": "At errorlevel=0, extraction continues after a filter refusal.", "reasoning": "At errorlevel=0, a filter refusal is logged, the member is skipped, and extraction continues.", "verdict": "SUPPORTED"}, {"citations": [{"index": 1, "quote": "Note that when extraction is aborted, :meth:`~TarFile.extractall` may leave\n    the archive partially extracted. It does not attempt to clean up."}], "claim_text": "If extractall is aborted, it automatically cleans up any partially extracted files.", "reasoning": "Jev decision summary (template): selected quotations from passage indices 1 jointly directly refute the full claim under the quote-only check.", "verdict": "CONTRADICTED"}, {"citations": [{"index": 4, "quote": "Even with ``filter='data'``, *tarfile* is not suited f